# Requests of lab 3.2 (REV-2), in the order of "Check it" in the lab booklet.
# Start first: your review-service, started fresh.
@reviewUrl = http://localhost:8083

### A review for event 1
POST {{reviewUrl}}/api/events/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"author": "Alice", "stars": 4, "text": "Great evening, good sound."}

### GET the Location
GET {{reviewUrl}}/api/reviews/1

### PUT on the Location: 3 stars, a new text
PUT {{reviewUrl}}/api/reviews/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"stars": 3, "text": "Good, but too short."}

### PUT on the Location: 2 stars, no text
PUT {{reviewUrl}}/api/reviews/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"stars": 2}

### PUT on an unknown review
PUT {{reviewUrl}}/api/reviews/999
Content-Type: application/json

{"stars": 4}

### GET an unknown review
GET {{reviewUrl}}/api/reviews/999

### Empty author, 6 stars
POST {{reviewUrl}}/api/events/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"author": "", "stars": 6}

### Ben, 1 star, no text
POST {{reviewUrl}}/api/events/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"author": "Ben", "stars": 1}

### Cleo, 5 stars, no text
POST {{reviewUrl}}/api/events/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"author": "Cleo", "stars": 5}

### After a restart: review 1
GET {{reviewUrl}}/api/reviews/1
